{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Inheritance", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear and use when talking about inheritance. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations. Talk about particular topics related to software programming.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. \t  Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "subclass ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "A subdivision of a set of classes.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This inherited class is called a subclass.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "implementation ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the act of putting something into practice.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Inheritance is basing an object or class on another object by using the same one or by identifying a new implementation to maintain the same behavior. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "behavioral ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "how something acts.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It doesn't even ensure a behavioral subtyping. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "single ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that is not related to others.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There is the single inheritance, where the class gets the properties of another class.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "assist ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to contribute or support another process.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's when one class assists as a superclass. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "feature", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a characteristic of something or somebody.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Inheritance is just a feature of this paradigm. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le03ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Investigate about the difference between inheritance and subtyping ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write your findingsin your notebook about the difference between inheritance and subtyping ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your findings about the difference between inheritance and subtyping with your classmates and teacher", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I investigate about the difference between inheritance and subtyping ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about the difference between inheritance and subtyping ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about the difference between inheritance and subtyping", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Used to ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<strong>Used to</strong> expresses an idea of a past habit. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The expression <strong>used to</strong> expresses the idea that someone had a habit or a recurrent action in the past, which is no longer happening in the present. You can also use it to describe the reality in the past, without making reference to a specific action of a person. </br>  The structure for creating sentences with this expression is the following:</br></br>  <div align=\"center\">Subject + <strong>used to</strong> + verb (base form) + complement.</div></br>  Example: </br> We <strong>used to</strong> use this software programming system 5 years ago. (regular action in the past)  </br> </br> That system <strong>used to</strong> be the best one available in the market. (description of the past reality)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I used to think that the term inheritance did not apply to programming languages.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I used to believe that inheritance created a semantic relationship. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I used to know about hierarchical inheritance, but I don't remember well.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Gerunds vs Infinitives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A verb in <strong>gerund</strong> is a verb in its \u201cing\u201d form. An <strong>infinitive</strong> verb is a verb formed with the preposition \u201cto\u201d plus the base form of the verb. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are different uses for gerund verbs and infinitives:</br></br> <strong>GERUNDS:</strong></br></br>  They can appear at the beginning of a sentence, used as a subject.</br></br>  Example:</br><i> <strong>Designing</strong> new programs can be expensive.</i></br></br> They can be the object following the verb.</br></br>  Example:</br><i> He quitted <strong>working</strong> in this company. </i></br></br> They can be used after certain verbs (love, hate, enjoy, etc\u2026)</br></br>  Example:</br><i> I love <strong>making</strong> new projects. </I After prepositions.</br> </br><i> I'm good at <strong>working</strong> with objects. </i></br></br>  <strong>INFINITIVES:</strong></br></br>   Us them as objects following the verb.</br></br>  Example:</br> <i> I forgot <strong>to call</strong> the new software programmer. </i></br></br>They are also used as a subject at the beginning of a sentence.</br></br>  Example:</br><i> <strong>To create</strong> a new software is crucial for the company. </i></br></br> Some verbs are followed by a noun or pronoun and then by an infinitive.</br></br>  Example:</br><i> He advised me <strong>to sell</strong> the software. </i>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Inheritance is basing an object or class on another object by using the same one or by identifying a new implementation to maintain the same behavior. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "To relate objects or classes through inheritance creates hierarchy. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Mixing two or more types of inheritance is called hybrid inheritance. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "What is a compound noun?", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A <strong>compound noun</strong> is a noun that is formed by two or more words.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A <strong>compound noun</strong> is usually formed with these combinations:</br></br>  <ul><li>Noun + noun (football) </li> <li>Adjective + noun (software)</li> <li>Verb + noun (swimming pool)</li> <li>Verb + preposition (check-out)</li> <li>Noun + prepositional phrase (mother-in-law)</li> <li>Preposition + noun (underworld)</li></ul></br>  A <strong>compound noun</strong> acts as a single unit and can be modified by adjectives and other nouns.</br></br>  There are three forms for compound nouns:</br></br>  1. Open or spaced - space between words </br> 2. Hyphenated - hyphen between words </br> 3. Closed or solid - no space or hyphen between words</br>", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can explain the concept of inheritance.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can give detailed information about inheritance. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about the relation between object-oriented programming.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What are the benefits of object oriented programming?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "How do you think objects in OOP work?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Talking About Computer Programming", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "type": "WLC"}, {"questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 1, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Studying for the Test About Inheritance", "t